==Strategy==
As the final challenge of Billionaire's Bidding, this stage pulls no punches. With Bun Bun Black, Aku Gory, and Midnite D. demanding a consistent stream of meatshields, Tackey in the backline, and Gobble denying [[Uril]]. Expect the stage name to ring true as you burn through your wallet dealing with these threats. Fortunately, the magnifications on this stage are (relatively) tame. The general idea is to stall until your Mythic Cats take down the main threats, and pray that they can take out the base before they get killed by brollows. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] can help with the Aku Gories and Bun-Bun Black, while [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman]] deals with the Brollows and Gobbles. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat ]] is useful as always to snipe Tackey. Use your strong backliners like [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Mina]], [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Naala]], [[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Nova]], or [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] to keep everything in check. Uril can work if you have something to deal with the Gobbles' Toxic.

If you have any ubers that outrange Gobble and can target any of these traits, use them.

Also note, be careful when meatshielding. Thanks to the gimmick of these stages, meatshielding can quickly become unsustainable in prolonged battles like these. Manage your money well, and you will make it back tenfold. Good luck!

